          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            The term ‘Lebesgue space’ can stand for two distinct notions: one is the general notion of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/measure+space"} measure space
            (compare the
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "http://eom.springer.de/L/l057910.htm"} Springer Encyclopaedia of Mathematics
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi L
                    %mi p
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L^p
            space (or
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi L
                    %mi p
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L_p
            space). Here we discuss the latter.
          %p
            Lebesgue spaces
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi L
                    %mi p
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L^p
            in this sense are
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/normed+vector+spaces"} normed vector spaces
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functions"} functions
            on a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/measure+space"} measure space
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/p-norm"} p-norm
          %p
            Beware that sometimes the notation ‘
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi L
                    %mi p
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L_p
            ’ is used as a synonym for
            = succeed ";" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi L
                      %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L^p
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi L
                      %mrow
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L^{1/p}
          %h2#notation Notation
          %p
            For historical reasons (starting with the original paper by Riesz), the exponent
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi p
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
            is traditionally taken to be the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reciprocal"} reciprocal
            of the “correct” exponent.
          %p
            If we take
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi M
                      %mi p
                    %mo =
                    %msup
                      %mi L
                      %mrow
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M^p=L^{1/p}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi M
                    %mi p
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M^p
            form a
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{C}
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/graded+algebra"} graded algebra
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{C}
            denotes
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+numbers"} complex numbers
          %p
            This is a conceptual explanation for the appearance of formulas like
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi p
                  %mo +
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi q
                  %mo =
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi r
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1/p+1/q=1/r
            in
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/H%C3%B6lder%27s+inequality"} Hölder's inequality
          %p
            In
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+geometry"} differential geometry
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/density"} density
            does use the “correct” grading.
          %p
            In the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tomita%E2%80%93Takesaki+theory"} Tomita–Takesaki theory
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi t
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t
            for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/modular+automorphism+group"} modular automorphism group
            is almost the “correct” grading, except that it is multiplied by the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/imaginary+unit"} imaginary unit
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i
          %h2#Definition Definitions
          %p
            If
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 1
                  %mo ≤
                  %mi p
                  %mo &lt;
                  %mn ∞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1 \leq p \lt \infty
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+number"} real number
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Ω
                  %mo ,
                  %mi μ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\Omega,\mu)
            is a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/measure+space"} measure space
            %strong
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi L
                      %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L^p
              space
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi L
                      %mi p
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Ω
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L_p(\Omega)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+space"} vector space
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+classes"} equivalence classes
            of those
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/measurable+function"} measurable
            (complex- or real-valued) functions
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi Ω
                  %mo →
                  %mi 𝕂
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f\colon \Omega \to \mathbb{K}
            whose (absolute values of)
            = succeed "th" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/integration"} integral
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                    %mi f
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                      %mi p
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ≔
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %msup
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %mstyle{:displaystyle => "false"}
                        %msub
                          %mo ∫
                          %mi Ω
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                          %mi f
                          %msup
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                            %mi p
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mi d
                        %mi μ
                      %mo )
                    %mrow
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mi p
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo &lt;
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mn ∞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  {\|f\|_p}
                  \\;\coloneqq\;
                  \\left(
                  \\textstyle{\int}_\Omega {|f|^p} \,d\mu
                  \\right)^{1/p}
                  \\;\lt\;
                  \\infty
          %p
            exists. Two such are taken to be equivalent,
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo ∼
                    %mi g
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \sim g
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                      %mi f
                      %mo −
                      %mi g
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                        %mi p
                    %mo =
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {\|f-g\|_p} = 0
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi p
                  %mo =
                  %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p = 2
            this is the space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi L
                    %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L^2
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/square+integrable+functions"} square integrable functions
          %p
            On these spaces
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi L
                    %mi p
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L^p(X)
            of equivalence classes of
            = succeed "-power" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                    %mi f
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                      %mi p
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {\|f\|_p}
            satisfies the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/triangle+inequality"} triangle inequality
            (due to
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Minkowski%27s+inequality"} Minkowski's inequality
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#MinkowskiInequality"} below
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/norm"} norm
            = succeed "," do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/p-norm"} p-norm
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/normed+vector+spaces"} normed vector spaces
          %p
            The
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi L
                    %mi p
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L^p
            spaces are examples of
            = succeed ";" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Banach+spaces"} Banach spaces
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi l
                    %mi p
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} l^p
            spaces of
            = succeed "-summable" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi l
                      %mi p
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi S
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} l^p(S)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/set"} set
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi L
                    %mi p
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi S
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L^p(S)
            if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            is equipped with
            = succeed ".)" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/counting+measure"} counting measure
          %p
            For fixed
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                    %mi f
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                      %mi p
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {\|f\|_p}
            is continuous in
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                    %mo =
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p = \infty
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                    %mi p
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {\|f\|}_p
            as
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                    %mo →
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p \to \infty
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/essential+supremum"} essential supremum
            norm
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                    %mi f
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                      %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \|f\|_\infty
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi L
                    %mn ∞
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Ω
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L^\infty(\Omega)
            makes sense as long as
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Ω
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/measurable+space"} measurable space
            equipped with a family of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/null+sets"} null sets
            (or
            = succeed ");" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+sets"} full sets
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi μ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mu
            is otherwise irrelevant.
          %p
            For
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 0
                    %mo ≤
                    %mi p
                    %mo &lt;
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0 \leq p \lt 1
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi L
                    %mi p
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L^p
            into an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/F-space"} F-space
            (but not a Banach space). See the definitions at
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/p-norm"} p-norm
          %h2#MinkowskiInequality Minkowski’s inequality
          %p
            We offer here a proof that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                    %mi f
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                      %mi p
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {\|f\|_p}
            indeed defines a norm in the case
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 1
                    %mo &lt;
                    %mi p
                    %mo &lt;
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1 \lt p \lt \infty
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/triangle+inequality"} triangle inequality
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Minkowski%27s+inequality"} Minkowski's inequality
          %p
            (The cases
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi p
                  %mo =
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p = 1
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi p
                  %mo =
                  %mn ∞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p = \infty
            follow by continuity and are easy to check from first principles.)
          %p
            The most usual textbook proofs involve a clever application of
            = succeed ";" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/H%C3%B6lder%27s+inequality"} Hölder's inequality
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            may be assumed to be real- or complex-valued.
          .num_theorem
            %h6#theorem Theorem
            %p
              Suppose
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn 1
                      %mo ≤
                      %mi p
                      %mo ≤
                      %mn ∞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1 \leq p \leq \infty
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Ω
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/measure+space"} measure space
              with
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/measure"} measure
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi μ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mu
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mi p
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %msup
                      %mi L
                      %mi p
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Ω
                    %mo ,
                    %mi μ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi ℝ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {|(-)|_p} \,\colon\, L^p(\Omega, \mu) \to \mathbb{R}
              defined by
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                      %mi f
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                        %mi p
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ≔
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                    %mstyle{:displaystyle => "false"}
                      %msub
                        %mo ∫
                        %mi Ω
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mi f
                        %msup
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                          %mi p
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mi d
                      %mi μ
                      %msup
                        %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                        %mrow
                          %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                          %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    {\|f\|_p}
                    \\;\coloneqq\;
                    \\big(
                    \\textstyle{\int}_\Omega {|f|^p} \,d\mu
                    \\big)^{1/p}
            %p
              defines a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/norm"} norm
          %p One must verify three things:
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                Separation axiom:
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                        %mi f
                        %msub
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                          %mi p
                      %mo =
                      %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {\|f\|_p} = 0
                implies
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi f
                        %mo =
                        %mn 0
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f = 0
            %li
              %p
                Scaling axiom:
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                            %mi t
                            %mi f
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                          %mi p
                        %mo =
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                          %mi t
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                          %mi f
                          %msub
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                            %mi p
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {\|t f\|}_p = {|t|} \, {\|f\|_p}
            %li
              %p
                Triangle inequality:
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                          %mi f
                          %mo +
                          %mi g
                          %msub
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                            %mi p
                        %mo ≤
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                          %mi f
                          %msub
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                            %mi p
                        %mo +
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                          %mi g
                          %msub
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                            %mi p
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {\|f + g\|_p} \leq {\|f\|_p} + {\|g\|_p}
          %p
            The first two properties are obvious, so it remains to prove the last, which is also called
            = succeed "." do
              %strong
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Minkowski%27s+inequality"} Minkowski's inequality
          %p
            Our proof of Minkowski’s inequality is broken down into a series of simple lemmas. The plan is to boil it down to two things: the scaling axiom, and convexity of the function
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                  %mo ↦
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mi x
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mi p
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \mapsto {|x|^p}
            (as a function from real or complex numbers to nonnegative real numbers).
          %p
            First, some generalities. Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            be a (real or complex) vector space equipped with a function
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi V
                  %mo →
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mn 0
                  %mo ,
                  %mn ∞
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {\|(-)\|}\colon V \to [0, \infty]
            that satisfies the scaling axiom:
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                    %mi t
                    %mi v
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                  %mo =
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mi t
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                    %mi v
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {\|t v\|} = {|t|} \, {\|v\|}
            for all scalars
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi t
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                    %mi v
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                  %mo =
                  %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {\|v\|} = 0
            implies
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi v
                    %mo =
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} v = 0
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unit+ball"} unit ball
            in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            to be
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mi v
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi V
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                    %mi v
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                  %mo ≤
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{v \in V \;|\; {\|v\|} \leq 1\}.
          #conditions.num_lemma
            %h6#lemma Lemma
            %p Given that the scaling and separation axioms hold, the following conditions are equivalent:
            %ol
              %li The triangle inequality is satisfied.
              %li The unit ball is convex.
              %li
                If
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                          %mi u
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                        %mo =
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                          %mi v
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                        %mo =
                        %mn 1
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {\|u\|} = {\|v\|} = 1
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                        %mi t
                        %mi u
                        %mo +
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mn 1
                        %mo −
                        %mi t
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mi v
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                      %mo ≤
                      %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {\|t u + (1-t)v\|} \leq 1
                for all
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi t
                        %mo ∈
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mn 0
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t \in [0, 1]
          .proof
            %h6#proof Proof
            %p
              Condition 1. implies condition 2. easily: if
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi u
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} u
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi v
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} v
              are in the unit ball and
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn 0
                      %mo ≤
                      %mi t
                      %mo ≤
                      %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0 \leq t \leq 1
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mrow
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                              %mi t
                              %mi u
                              %mo +
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mn 1
                              %mo −
                              %mi t
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mi v
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                          %mtd
                            %mo ≤
                          %mtd
                            %mrow
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                              %mi t
                              %mi u
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                            %mo +
                            %mrow
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mn 1
                              %mo −
                              %mi t
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mi v
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo =
                          %mtd
                            %mi t
                            %mrow
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                              %mi u
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                            %mo +
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mn 1
                            %mo −
                            %mi t
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mrow
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                              %mi v
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo ≤
                          %mtd
                            %mi t
                            %mo +
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mn 1
                            %mo −
                            %mi t
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo =
                            %mn 1
                            %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    {\|t u + (1-t)v\|} &amp; \leq &amp; {\|t u\|} + {\|(1-t)v\|} \\
                    \&amp; = &amp; t {\|u\|} + (1-t) {\|v\|} \\
                    \&amp; \leq &amp; t + (1-t) = 1.}
            %p
              Now 2. implies 3. trivially, so it remains to prove that 3. implies 1. Suppose
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                        %mi v
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                      %mo ,
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                        %mi v
                        %mo ′
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                      %mo ∈
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 0
                      %mo ,
                      %mn ∞
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {\|v\|}, {\|v'\|} \in (0, \infty)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi u
                    %mo =
                    %mfrac
                      %mi v
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                        %mi v
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} u = \frac{v}{{\|v\|}}
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi u
                    %mo ′
                    %mo =
                    %mfrac
                      %mrow
                        %mi v
                        %mo ′
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                        %mi v
                        %mo ′
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} u' = \frac{v'}{{\|v'\|}}
              be the associated unit vectors. Then
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mfrac
                              %mrow
                                %mi v
                                %mo +
                                %mi v
                                %mo ′
                              %mrow
                                %mrow
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                                  %mi v
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                                %mo +
                                %mrow
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                                  %mi v
                                  %mo ′
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                          %mtd
                            %mo =
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mfrac
                              %mrow
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                                %mi v
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                              %mrow
                                %mrow
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                                  %mi v
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                                %mo +
                                %mrow
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                                  %mi v
                                  %mo ′
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mfrac
                              %mi v
                              %mrow
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                                %mi v
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                            %mo +
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mfrac
                              %mrow
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                                %mi v
                                %mo ′
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                              %mrow
                                %mrow
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                                  %mi v
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                                %mo +
                                %mrow
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                                  %mi v
                                  %mo ′
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mfrac
                              %mrow
                                %mi v
                                %mo ′
                              %mrow
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                                %mi v
                                %mo ′
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo =
                          %mtd
                            %mi t
                            %mi u
                            %mo +
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mn 1
                            %mo −
                            %mi t
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mi u
                            %mo ′
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    \\frac{v + v'}{{\|v\|}+{\|v'\|}} &amp; = &amp; (\frac{{\|v\|}}{{\|v\|}+{\|v'\|}})\frac{v}{{\|v\|}} + (\frac{{\|v'\|}}{{\|v\|}+{\|v'\|}})\frac{v'}{{\|v'\|}} \\
                    \&amp; = &amp; t u + (1-t)u'}
            %p
              where
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi t
                      %mo =
                      %mfrac
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                          %mi v
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                        %mrow
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                            %mi v
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                          %mo +
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                            %mi v
                            %mo ′
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t = \frac{{\|v\|}}{{\|v\|} + {\|v'\|}}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                      %mi t
                      %mi u
                      %mo +
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 1
                      %mo −
                      %mi t
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi u
                      %mo ′
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                    %mo ≤
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {\|t u + (1-t)u'\|} \leq 1
            %p but by the scaling axiom, this is the same as saying
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mfrac
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                        %mi v
                        %mo +
                        %mi v
                        %mo ′
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                      %mrow
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                          %mi v
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                        %mo +
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                          %mi v
                          %mo ′
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                    %mo ≤
                    %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \frac{{\|v + v'\|}}{{\|v\|} + {\|v'\|}} \leq 1,
            %p which is the triangle inequality.
          %p
            Consider now
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi L
                    %mi p
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L^p
            with its
            = succeed "-norm" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                    %mo =
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mi f
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {\|f\|} = {|f|_p}
            = succeed "," do
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#conditions"}
          %ul
            %li
              %strong Condition 4:
              If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mi u
                      %msubsup
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mi p
                        %mi p
                    %mo =
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {|u|_{p}^{p}} = 1
              and
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mi v
                        %msubsup
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                          %mi p
                          %mi p
                      %mo =
                      %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {|v|_{p}^{p}} = 1
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mi t
                      %mi u
                      %mo +
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 1
                      %mo −
                      %mi t
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi v
                      %msubsup
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mi p
                        %mi p
                    %mo ≤
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {|t u + (1-t)v|_{p}^{p}} \leq 1
              whenever
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn 0
                      %mo ≤
                      %mi t
                      %mo ≤
                      %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0 \leq t \leq 1
          %p
            This allows us to remove the cumbersome exponent
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 1
